[[48,96,16,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"removing\" data-part=\"removal\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"refitting\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</a><p>Place the vehicle on a lift.</p><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/768.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2000166.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th colspan=\"1\"><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/767.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><p>Follow the safety instructions\n(See 5040A - Precautions)</p></aside></th></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"1\"></td></tr></table></div></aside><p>Drain the coolant (\n                                          <a href=\"#/3238305\">5040A10</a>\n                                           ).</p><p>1. Working on the right side of the engine compartment, disconnect\nthe coupling for the pipes from the evaporator to the compressor.</p><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/769.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2000041.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th colspan=\"1\"><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/767.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><p>Seal the disconnected connectors,\nusing suitable plugs, to prevent humidity and impurities from entering\nthe system.</p></aside></th></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"1\"></td></tr></table></div></aside><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2018466.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[48,96,16,"<p><a href=\"#/3238966\">7055B54</a></p><p>1. Disconnect the couplings for the compressor pipes.</p><p>2. Remove the pipe from the connector for the pipe between the evaporator\nand the compressor.</p><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2018467.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[48,96,16,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"refitting\" data-part=\"refit\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"removing\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</a><p>Check that the pipe is not damaged and\nthat there are no cracks which would affect the seal.</p><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/769.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2000041.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th colspan=\"1\"><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/767.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><p>Replace the O-rings for the connectors\nand lubricate the connector threads using anti-freeze. Only use\ngreen coloured seals, resistant to R134A coolant fluid.</p></aside></th></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"1\"></td></tr></table></div></aside><p>Position the pipe and connect the couplings\nfor the compressor pipes.</p><p><a href=\"#/3238966\">7055B54</a>\n                                           .</p><p>Connect the coupling for the pipes from\nthe evaporator to the compressor.</p><p>Repressurize using coolant fluid (\n                                          <a href=\"#/3238305\">5040A10</a>\n                                           ).</p><p>Remove the vehicle from the lift.</p>"]]